Subject: [PATCH 05533/11362] [outer-loop] add QA-Layer Authenticity
 Discipline: the auditor now has an auditor

Operator, after digging into 4 real bugs found in scripts/adversarial_verify.py
today: 'are all of these fixes due to using sonnet 5 instead of opus 4.8?
shouldn't the adversarial agent be catching these?' Investigated honestly:
no, not the model swap (every bug predated it or was in codex-authored
artifacts, unrelated to the planner). But the second question was right --
there's a real, standing gap. Confirmed by checking existing audit scope:
verifier_authenticity_audit.py covers python/carnot/verify/*.py only;
pages_adversarial_audit.py covers docs/index.html only. The mechanical
fabrication-detection/gate/reconciliation layer itself (adversarial_verify.py,
exclusion_manifest_lint.py, in_process_doc_reconcile.py) was outside every
existing audit's scope by design. Nobody polices the auditor.

Added scripts/qa_layer_authenticity_audit.py, sibling to
verifier_authenticity_audit.py, reusing its battle-tested pattern (call_gemini/
call_claude/call_codex dispatch, structured VERDICT/FINDINGS output, the
audit-integrity Layer-1.5 guard that fact-checks the LLM reviewer's own quoted
evidence against the real source so a hallucinated smoking gun auto-downgrades
to CANNOT_DETERMINE instead of being acted on). Two audit granularities:
whole-file for the two small targets, function-level chunking (via ast) for
adversarial_verify.py (5685 lines, far too large for a single-shot audit to
stay focused) -- extracts every top-level function, filters to the 152 whose
body does field extraction or string pattern-matching (the exact bug class
already found), audits each independently. Added persisted rotation state
(ops/.qa_layer_audit_rotation.json, gitignored, mirrors ops/.pretest-cache.json's
precedent) so successive --limit 20 milestone-close runs advance through the
whole 154-unit corpus over time instead of always re-auditing the same
head-slice -- the unaddressed limitation the sibling audit still has.

Wired into research_conductor.py's milestone-close path alongside the
existing two audits (same AGENT_TYPE_AUDIT/AGENT_MODEL_AUDIT routing, same
non-fatal try/except, same --limit 20 bound).

Live-tested end-to-end with codex before wiring (claude was contended --
the conductor's own verifier-authenticity audit was running concurrently at
milestone-close, correctly left undisturbed). First real run found a genuine,
well-evidenced issue on the first unit scanned: exclusion_manifest_lint.py's
BLOCKED_PATTERN_MATCHED check has the same two bug classes already fixed
elsewhere today (raw substring matching with no word-boundary awareness;
principle-wrapped id/requires/operator_override/title/prompt fields not
unwrapped), plus negation handling that's only wired for the KV260 check, not
blocked_patterns generally. Included a concrete, plausible counterexample
(a roadmap task explicitly guarding against FoVer premise reuse gets
wrongly blocked because its own prompt text names the retired phrase).
Not yet acted on -- flagging for the operator per the discipline's own
'audit never edits, operator decides' contract. Report committed as-is
(ops/qa_layer_authenticity_audit_report.md), matching the tracked-in-git
precedent of the sibling audit reports.

17 new tests (tests/python/test_qa_layer_authenticity_audit.py) covering the
pure-logic pieces: function-chunk extraction (risky-marker filtering, nested-
function handling, tiny-function floor, syntax-error/missing-file handling),
verdict parsing, the audit-integrity guard (including a fix discovered while
writing the test -- the specificity regex was missing np.random/time.sleep/
torch.load patterns the sibling audit's own regex has, narrowing coverage
unintentionally when I adapted it), and rotation-state wraparound math.
LLM-CLI subprocess wrappers (call_claude/call_gemini/call_codex) are
untested by design, matching the sibling script's own precedent -- they
require live external CLIs and are exercised by use.

Documented as a new MANDATORY CLAUDE.md discipline (three-layer structure
mirroring Verifier Authenticity and Adversarial Landing-Page: Layer 1
deliberately absent since the target files ARE the mechanical-lint layer,
Layer 2 the new AI audit, Layer 3 this rule), added to the Rule Index.

Full suite: 271 tests green (254 adversarial_verify + 17 new).

